<article class="env-corollary" id="06Z2">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06Z2">Corollary <span data-tag="06Z2">9.4.3.15</span>.</a> Let $n \geq 0$ be a nonnegative integer. Then $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}^{\leq n}_{\mathrm{fin}}$ is the smallest full subcategory of $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}^{\leq n}$ which is closed under finite colimits and contains the standard $1$-simplex $\Delta ^1$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}^{\leq n}_{0} \subseteq \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}^{\leq n}$ be the smallest full subcategory which contains $\Delta ^1$ and is closed under finite colimits; we wish to show that $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}^{\leq n}_{\mathrm{fin}}$ is contained in $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}^{\leq n}_{0}$ (the reverse inclusion follows from Proposition <a data-tag="06Z1" href="/tag/06Z1">9.4.3.14</a>). Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_0 \subseteq \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}$ be the full subcategory spanned by those $\infty $-categories $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ satisfying $\operatorname {h}_{\mathit{\leq {}n}}{\mathit{(\operatorname{\mathcal{D}})}} \in \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}^{\leq n}_{0}$. Then $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_0$ contains $\Delta ^1$ and is closed under finite colimits, and therefore contains all essentially finite $\infty $-categories (Proposition <a data-tag="068E" href="/tag/068E">9.2.7.8</a>). If $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ belongs to $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}^{\leq n}_{\mathrm{fin}}$, then $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is equivalent to $\operatorname {h}_{\mathit{\leq {}n}}{\mathit{(\operatorname{\mathcal{D}})}}$ for some essentially finite $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$, so that $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\in \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}^{\leq n}_{0}$ as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
